ly.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Connecticut enters the 2028 presidential contest with an eight-point Democratic lean and no incumbent on the ballot, since the term-limited president leaves office. No general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices are available yet, so the outlook rests on the state's fundamental partisan balance. Connecticut has backed Democrats consistently in recent presidential elections, and nothing in the current evidence points to a shift.\n\nThe race sits in Lean Democratic territory with a wide uncertainty band because direct polling is absent and the national climate could still move. Primary-season headlines, including jockeying among Connecticut Democrats ahead of 2028, do not change the general-election picture. A Democratic win is more likely than not, but the margin could swing several points either way with turnout and the national environment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8243, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.781, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7754, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7619, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7738, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7843, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7768, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7843, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7811, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7718, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7751, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7661, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7723, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7668, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7815, "margin": 8.0}]}